== Personal life ==
Rhoden lives in [[Union Center, South Dakota]]. He and his wife, Sandy, have four children and seven grandchildren.<ref name=gov_off>{{cite web|date=January 25, 2025|title=South Dakota Governor|url= https://governor.sd.gov/governor/about.aspx}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=The Governor's Team |url=https://governor.sd.gov/office/team.aspx |website=governor.sd.gov |access-date=January 26, 2025}}</ref> Rhoden is a rancher by trade and runs and owns a cow-calf operation and custom welding business.<ref name="ballotpedia.org"/><ref name="Sioux">{{cite news|last=Hayworth|first=Bret|date=July 10, 2013|title=Politically Speaking: Rhoden enters S.D. Senate race, setting GOP primary with Mike Rounds|newspaper=Sioux City Journal|url=http://siouxcityjournal.com/blogs/politically_speaking/politically-speaking-rhoden-enters-s-d-senate-race-setting-gop/article_8e095bb1-aa8a-516f-9afb-f418a912ff0c.html|access-date=August 16, 2013}}</ref>

